{
  "note": [
    "A CENSUS OF THE LIVE CHAIN \u2014 the independent oracle for the board fee-delivery cut.",
    "",
    "Not a list written here and not a restatement of the script: Base Sepolia's own answer to",
    "'which selectors are mounted in the diamond today', read through the loupe with",
    "  cast call $DIAMOND_ADDRESS \"facets()((address,bytes4[])[])\"",
    "The composition of the cut (script/UpgradeBoardFeeDelivery.s.sol) is held against",
    "THIS, never against itself.",
    "",
    "WHY IT MATTERS FOR THIS ONE. The cut REPLACES three whole facets and ADDS two",
    "selectors, so it can meet BOTH halves of the pair that drops a cut on one live",
    "transaction: Replace reverts 'Diamond: selector not found' on a selector that is",
    "not mounted, Add reverts 'Diamond: selector exists' on one that is. Three claims",
    "have to be proved, and none may be taken from the script:",
    "",
    "  * every selector the three rebuilt facets expose, EXCEPT the two new ones, is",
    "    mounted today -> it belongs in Replace;",
    "  * every selector mounted on those three facets today is still exposed by the",
    "    rebuilt facets -> nothing is left pointing at code that no longer implements it;",
    "  * the two new FactoryFacet selectors are mounted NOWHERE in the diamond ->",
    "    they belong in Add, and the whole routed list below is what makes that a",
    "    statement about the diamond rather than about one facet.",
    "",
    "The other side of all three comparisons is solc's own methodIdentifiers, read out",
    "of the build artifacts. Neither side is computed from the other.",
    "",
    "STATE OF THE CHAIN WHEN THIS WAS TAKEN. 13 facets, 214 routed selectors, zero",
    "unrecognised: every mounted selector maps to a contract whose source is in src/.",
    "The three facets below were additionally compared byte for byte against the",
    "locally built artifacts (deployedBytecode minus the trailing CBOR metadata) and",
    "matched, so 'what is mounted' and 'what the tree compiles' were the same code on",
    "the day this census was read."
  ],
